WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:03.103
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.009
- So you live half the
time right here in Israel

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.044
and half the time in Florida.

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I don't know that
there's ever been a guest

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.248
that I'm supposed
to sit down with

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Jerusalem in this
exact spot more than you.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.252
But I want to actually
start somewhere else

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.955
for just a minute or so,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:25.191
because you also grew
up in Long Island,

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.894
like basically 10 minutes
from where I grew up from.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.428
- That's right.

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:30.630
- And I thought for people
that don't know your bio,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
could you give just
sort of a one-minute bio

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:34.801
that'll then get us
to to everything else
that you've done?

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.636
- Sure, son of a rabbi.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.839
Thought about becoming a rabbi.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
My father had a
1,000-member congregation.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.676
He was a great rabbi.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.780 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I told him I was
thinking of becoming a rabbi,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.248
he cried.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.549
He begged me not to do it.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.484
- (laughs) I was gonna
say, tears of joy or-

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.752
- No, no, not tears of joy.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.187
He was like, "Why would
you want to do that?"

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.488 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's a tough gig.
- "Be a doctor or a lawyer,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.024 align:start size:88% position:13%
make some money and
don't have 1,000 bosses

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.426
telling you what to do,"

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.926
even though he loved his job.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:03.930 align:start size:97% position:3%
Sent me off to Columbia
University, became a lawyer.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.298
Lived basically in the
area where I grew up

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:07.500
for most of my life,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.735
until I became the U.S.
Ambassador to Israel

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:13.039
and moved here in 2017.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.841
- Okay, so you probably

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:18.378
are the most influential
U.S. ambassador to Israel

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably in its existence,
I mean, I know...

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.447
Do you want to pat
yourself on the back?

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:22.448
Is that fair to say,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean?
- Well, put it this way.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
"The New York Times" said
that, and they're no fans, so.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:27.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
- (chuckles) Oh, so they
might have been sticking you

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:28.154
when they said that.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.388
- Well, they said that,

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
so we'll refer to
them for that, yeah.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.191
- So let's start

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.594
just with exactly where
we are at the moment,

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:39.666
and the incredible history and
geography of where we're at,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.135
before we get into some of
the politics of the region

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.670
that you've really helped shape,

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
which has clearly led to an
incredibly flourishing Israel.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.842
In my five days here, I can't
believe what's going on here.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.376
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, look, we're about a
10-minute walk from my home,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:58.151
and we are right here,
where that gold dome is,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.555
is the holiest place
for the Jewish people.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.458
It's now called the
Dome of the Rock.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.660 align:start size:81% position:19%
It was built maybe
1500 years ago.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:97% position:3%
But 3,000 years ago, it's
where the Jewish Temple stood.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.467
And that Temple stood
in two different forms,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.535
but it stood for 1,000 years.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.738
And it was destroyed the
second time in the year 70.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.607
And ever since then, until 1967,

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.542
the Jewish people
have been praying,

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:26.545 align:start size:88% position:13%
in every country,
whether it's, you know,

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:29.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
north Africa, eastern
Europe, the United States,

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:97% position:3%
for 2,000 years, Jews have
prayed to return to this land,

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.288
to return exactly to that spot.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.323
And in 1967, right
after the Six-Day War

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Jerusalem was
reunified, it came to be.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:44.297
So, you know, even though
this dome and this mosque

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.900
look very old, and they
are, relatively speaking,

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.036
they're pretty recent when
you think of Jewish history

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.771
that goes back 3500 years.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.873
- Right, so it's hard for
people to imagine, but,

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.542
because everyone thinks
that the Western Wall

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:88% position:13%
is actually the holiest
site in Judaism;

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's the Temple
Mount that the mosque,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.113
which is right there, and
then the Dome of the Rock,

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.515
are built on here.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.351 align:start position:0%
And the Western Wall is
actually just a retaining wall.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.786
- It's a retaining wall.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a lot bigger than
that; it goes much further.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:10.390
If you go underground, you
can see it goes further.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.791
But it's a retaining wall.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.627 align:start size:97% position:3%
The holiest site in Judaism
is the Temple Mount.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
It is under that, it's
called the Dome of the Rock

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:21.067
because the rock is the rock
on which Abraham was called

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.768
to sacrifice his son, Isaac,

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.471
and he passed the test that
was given to him by God,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.472
and God promised
that he'd become

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.807
the father of many nations.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.942
It all began there,
under that rock.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.144
And then, of course,

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.646
that's where Solomon
built the first Temple.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.381 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's enormously
important to Jews.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.916
And the proof of it is that,

00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:40.619
you know, for thousands of
years when we didn't have it,

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.555
we prayed for it.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
Look, the other thing
is if, you know,

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.091
you see the mosque to the right,

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:48.828
the Aqsa Mosque is the
silver mosque, right.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.162
- Right, that's this right here.

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:51.531
- So if you go into
the mosque and pray,

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.199
and you or I couldn't do that,

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.101
but if you went into
the mosque and prayed,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.370
you would bow down and
you would face south,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.638
you would face Mecca.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.273
Your back would be
to the Temple, okay.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.676
So the Temple is not,

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:07.246 align:start size:97% position:3%
even the holiness of
Jerusalem is very secondary

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.182 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the Muslim world, relative
to the holiness of Mecca.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, Jerusalem was
not mentioned in the Koran.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.789 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's mentioned 699 times
in the Old Testament.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.057
- And all that being said,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
all the religions
are being respected.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.360
You can see Muslim
worshipers, right?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.828 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- Literally right there.

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:24.530 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't know if they can
quite be seen by our camera.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.765
And then plenty of, obviously,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.266 align:start size:88% position:13%
of Jewish worshipers and
Christian worshipers.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It's actually more than
them being respected.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.235
Because, you know,

00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:31.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
you see here straight
ahead is the Western Wall,

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.672
up on top is the mosque,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.940 align:start size:97% position:3%
and to the left is the
Church of the Holy Sepulchre,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.410 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is one of the holiest
sites in Christianity.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.044
Now, if you're a Jew,
if you're a Muslim,

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:41.247
if you're a Christian,
if you're an atheist,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.049
you can go to the Church
of the Holy Sepulchre,

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.650
you can go to the Western Wall.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.852
If you want to go up on the
Temple Mount, all right,

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:49.221
and you're not a Muslim,
you have one access point,

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.791 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is this rickety gate
here called the Mughrabi Gate,

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.058
where you go through security.

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:55.427 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's 10 other
access for believers,

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:57.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, whet they refer
to as believers here,

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.631
which are just Muslims.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.399
And if you happen to
be a Jew or a Christian

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.335
and you go up through this
gate onto the Temple Mount

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:04.837
and you begin to pray,

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.339
you're escorted off the
mosque, off of the Mount.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:09.441
- The U.N. will write up
a couple recommendations.

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:11.811
- So it's not equal access,
it's actually better access.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.615
The state of Israel affords
better access to Muslims,

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.350
far better access to Muslims

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
than it does to
Christians and Jews.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.621
And it's odd, because, you know,

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's referred to generally
as the status quo.

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:26.926
But if you look at the treaty
between Jordan and Israel,

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.795 align:start size:81% position:19%
the treaty says
that both nations,

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.262
regardless of sovereignty,

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:32.465
will afford complete and
equal and unfettered access

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:35.535
to every Abrahamic faith
as to every holy site.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.604 align:start size:88% position:13%
And that's not done
here; it's not observed.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.972
- Right, so it's sort of ironic,

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.474
and then we'll move on
to some other stuff,

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:45.110
that Israel is actually
affording more courtesies

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.046
than was happening
before, you know-

00:05:48.046 --> 00:05:49.314 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- Israeli control, but.

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:52.151
- And Al-Aqsa has been
the theme since 1929,

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.086
when there was a
massacre in Hebron,

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.121
where hundreds of
Jews were killed.

00:05:56.121 --> 00:06:00.459 align:start size:97% position:3%
The false claim that the
Jews are storming the mosque,

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:01.727
taking over the mosque,

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.796
it's always been kind
of the rallying point

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
whenever Arab
terrorists have sought

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
to create violence
against the Jewish people.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:10.803
- All right, so let's,

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.238 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know we could do the
history clearly all day long,

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:14.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
for many days.
(Ambassador Friedman chuckles)

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.309 align:start size:97% position:3%
So let's get to the broader
Middle East, though.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:17.977 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Sure.
- Because you were integral

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
in what has happened
here over these last now,

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.248
you know, seven years or so.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:25.084
So talk to me about when
you became ambassador,

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.286 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, were you, was
that the immediate plan,

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.588 align:start size:81% position:19%
like, "We're gonna
do this stuff"?

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.222
Did it sort of fall in your lap,

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:32.625
and did you ever think
it was even possible?

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.626
- So, I was the first
ambassador appointed

00:06:34.626 --> 00:06:36.863
in the Trump administration,
even before he took office.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:38.531
And we put out a press release,

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:41.567
and I was quoted, with the
permission of the President,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:44.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
with saying that I look
forward to serving my country

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:47.273 align:start size:97% position:3%
from an embassy in its
eternal, undivided capital,

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
Jerusalem, in Israel's
undivided capital.

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:51.077
So this was number
one on my agenda.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.611
- Right, so that was
before the deals, even.

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.213
- That's before we
even took office.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.181
- Yeah.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.283
- We worked on it really hard.

00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:00.319
We, in less than a year,

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.622 align:start size:88% position:13%
the President recognized
Jerusalem as the
capital of Israel.

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:06.058
And then, May 14th

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:10.229
of 2018, exactly five years
ago this coming May 14th,

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:13.332
which is also Israel's
Day of Independence,

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.734
we opened up our embassy.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, you know, the
entire world predicted

00:07:17.335 --> 00:07:21.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
that this would create endless
wars and untold violence,

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it really
didn't, not at all.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.577 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No, there was
basically nothing.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.778 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Basically nothing,
and you know why?

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.480
Because everybody who's
looked at this knows

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Jerusalem is the
eternal, undivided capital

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:32.018
of the Jewish people.

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.352
I mean, you have to know it.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.854
If you, you read
the Bible, right?

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.489
The Bible sells more books on
Amazon than any other book.

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:38.023
Anybody who reads
the Bible knows

00:07:38.023 --> 00:07:39.692
that Jerusalem belongs
to the Jewish people,

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.627 align:start size:84% position:16%
including most of
the Christian world,

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.128
so, and most of
the Muslim world.

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:45.063 align:start size:88% position:13%
And most of the Muslims
actually consider,

00:07:45.063 --> 00:07:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, Mecca to be
holy, far less Jerusalem.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:50.402 align:start size:84% position:16%
So not surprisingly,
that's the least.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:51.337
There was at that time-

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:52.538
- So did that embolden you guys?

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.473
Once that was done and settled,

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.675
and it didn't inflame the
world, did then you go,

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:58.177
"Okay, now we can
really do some"-

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:01.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
- It gave us a real
tailwind in two respects.

00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:02.915 align:start size:84% position:16%
Number one, it
gave us the ability

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.850
to make more positive moves

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.186
that had been neglected for
years with regard to Israel.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:10.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
So recognized Israel's
sovereignty over
the Golan Heights,

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.258 align:start size:84% position:16%
which was never
gonna leave Israel,

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:13.392
was never gonna be given back

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.794
to a butcher like Bashar Assad.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:18.363 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then we started focusing
more on the Palestinians

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:19.631
and how to, you know,

00:08:19.631 --> 00:08:21.500
maybe choreograph some
sort of a peace plan.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.370
But what we found was, and I
think this is the key point,

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.471
people said, "You're gonna make,

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.172
you're gonna create violence

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:29.374
by supporting Israel and
supporting Jerusalem."

00:08:29.374 --> 00:08:30.809
Just to the contrary.

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:32.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we actually
created an environment of,

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.579 align:start size:81% position:19%
that was conducive
to peace. Why?

00:08:34.579 --> 00:08:36.949
Because the Arab nations that
we made peace with, right,

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
they looked at our
relationship with Israel,

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.719
and said, you know, "We
want to get in on that.

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:43.188
You know, we want to be an
ally of the United States

00:08:43.188 --> 00:08:44.623
the same way that
Israel's an ally.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:45.825
How do we get there?

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:47.293 align:start size:84% position:16%
How do we get closer
to each other?"

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.095 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you know, in
many cases, we said,

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.464
"Well, the road to that
kind of relationship

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:52.564
has to run through Israel.

00:08:52.564 --> 00:08:53.832 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have to normalize
with Israel.

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:56.435
You can't, you know,
be closer to America

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you're, you know,
shouting, 'Death to Israel'.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:01.206
You're fighting our
most important ally,

00:09:01.206 --> 00:09:03.508 align:start size:97% position:3%
maybe in the world, but
certainly in the Middle East."

00:09:03.508 --> 00:09:07.779 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, our closeness to
Israel was actually an asset

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.216
in our relationship
with the Arab world.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:11.683
And it drew us closer to them.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:16.155
And ultimately, you know, we
would sit with these countries,

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.956
it started off with the UAE,

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:22.094 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we said, "Look," you know,
and by the way, you know,

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:24.563
Trump said this on
his very first trip.

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:28.400
He went to Saudi Arabia, he
sat with 52 Muslim nations,

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.902
and he said something he
doesn't get credit for.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:33.238
He said, "Look, this idea that
Israel's gonna be destroyed,

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:34.506
put it out of your mind.

00:09:34.506 --> 00:09:35.708
Just forget about it.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.342 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's a pipe dream; it's
never gonna happen.

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:40.379
And it's gonna keep
you at distant, at
arms length with us."

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:41.814
That's number one.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.583 align:start size:97% position:3%
Number two, you know, "Radical
Islamic terrorism, okay,

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:45.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's your problem
first, not ours, okay.

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:48.554
You know, you stop it before
it crosses the Atlantic Ocean.

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:50.589
And if you do that, you
will find in America

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:53.025 align:start size:97% position:3%
a level of friendship you've
not experienced before."

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.293
So he actually set the tone,

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:55.795 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know, very
early in the term.

00:09:55.795 --> 00:09:57.997 align:start size:84% position:16%
But we worked on that
theme throughout.

00:09:57.997 --> 00:10:01.700
And as we got closer
to the end of the term,

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.269
we found these countries,
they saw a window closing.

00:10:04.269 --> 00:10:07.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
"How can we, you know, align
ourselves with America,

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:09.508 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, in a way that
starts to resemble, you know,

00:10:09.508 --> 00:10:10.443
this alliance with Israel?

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:11.977
How can we build this, you know,

00:10:11.977 --> 00:10:15.247
this kind of circle
of trust, you know,

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:17.650
around a common threat of Iran?"

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.352
And you know, it
involved, you know,

00:10:20.352 --> 00:10:23.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
some you know, fabulous
discussions, negotiations,

00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:24.657
and ultimately results.

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:25.991
- I don't know how much
you can say on this,

00:10:25.991 --> 00:10:27.193
but how close were you?

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:28.727 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, there were
all the rumors

00:10:28.727 --> 00:10:30.262
that there were gonna be all
these other rapprochements,

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:33.231 align:start position:0%
and obviously, you guys
literally just ran out of time.

00:10:33.231 --> 00:10:35.401 align:start size:88% position:13%
And now, unfortunately,
our administration

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:36.836
is looking at the Middle
East very differently.

00:10:36.836 --> 00:10:39.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, we would've
normalized with Saudi Arabia.

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:42.575 align:start size:97% position:3%
Saudi Arabia would've
normalized with Israel by now,

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:43.542
if we were still in.

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:46.846
It's a massive game changer.

00:10:46.846 --> 00:10:48.080 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, you're
talking about now,

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.615
the leader of the Muslim world.

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:50.983
- Right.

00:10:50.983 --> 00:10:51.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Normalizing this
relationship, it just changes,

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:54.520
it really ends, you know, ends,

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.690
just puts a period on the
Arab-Israeli conflict,

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.925 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it unites everyone
against radicalism.

00:10:59.925 --> 00:11:01.060
You know, when I met

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.530 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the foreign
minister of the UAE,

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.800
about six months after
the Abraham Accords,

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.001
there had been a war in Gaza.

00:11:10.001 --> 00:11:11.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're getting all their
news from Al Jazeera,

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:12.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is very
unfavorable to Israel.

00:11:12.938 --> 00:11:14.173
I sat and I met with him

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:15.574
and I said to him,
"How are we doing?"

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:17.843 align:start size:97% position:3%
He said, "No, we're passing
with flying colors."

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:19.011 align:start size:81% position:19%
And he said to me,
"You know why?"

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:21.213
And what he said to me was,

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:24.850
"The wars of the 21st century,"

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.318
now this was before
Russia and Ukraine,

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
which may be the exception
that proves the rule.

00:11:28.254 --> 00:11:29.655
But he says,

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:31.924 align:start size:97% position:3%
"The wars of the 21st
century are wars of ideology.

00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:33.926 align:start size:88% position:13%
They're not wars
between nations anymore.

00:11:33.926 --> 00:11:35.594
And the main ideological war

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:37.930 align:start size:84% position:16%
is extremism versus
the moderates.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:38.964
And the moderates have to win.

00:11:38.964 --> 00:11:40.366
And to us, the Abraham Accords

00:11:40.366 --> 00:11:42.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
is all about the moderates
winning the war."

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:45.604 align:start size:88% position:13%
- When you were, when
the whole administration

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:47.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
was, you know,
packing their bags,

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:49.008
and then there's
incoming people,

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:51.277 align:start size:97% position:3%
did you have any communication
with the incoming people,

00:11:51.277 --> 00:11:54.146 align:start position:0%
saying, "Hey guys," and I asked
Jared Kushner this as well,

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:56.649
"Hey, we're on the path here"?

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.217 align:start size:88% position:13%
Was there anything that
you could have done

00:11:58.217 --> 00:12:00.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
that would've
continued everything?

00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:03.088 align:start size:97% position:3%
And look, hopefully it'll
continue, maybe in two years.

00:12:03.088 --> 00:12:06.358
- Yeah, well look, for the
first six months, it was,

00:12:06.358 --> 00:12:09.495
anything Trump was,
you know, verboten.

00:12:09.495 --> 00:12:11.496
You know, no, we're not gonna...

00:12:11.496 --> 00:12:12.698 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then they
realized, you know,

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:14.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Abraham Accords
are so popular

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:16.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
among so many different
people, Democrats as well,

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:18.170
they began to embrace them.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:19.138 align:start size:81% position:19%
But it's not about
embracing them

00:12:19.138 --> 00:12:20.439
or paying lip service to it.

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:24.376 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's about being a
friend to Saudi Arabia.

00:12:24.376 --> 00:12:26.645
Now look, Saudi Arabia
is an imperfect country.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:28.080
There's no question about it.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.681 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they have that one
incident, which is horrific.

00:12:29.681 --> 00:12:30.782
But you know what?

00:12:30.782 --> 00:12:31.817
You know, you know,

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:35.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not gonna quote
Jesus because I'm Jewish.

00:12:35.955 --> 00:12:37.622
But you know,

00:12:37.622 --> 00:12:40.893
"Whoever's without sin,
you know, come forward,"

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:43.129
you know, and you're not,
no one's coming forward.

00:12:43.129 --> 00:12:44.796
Saudi Arabia could
be a very good friend

00:12:44.796 --> 00:12:46.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the United States; they
have been in the past.

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:48.067
We could advance
that relationship.

00:12:48.067 --> 00:12:50.102
And what Biden's done
really, has been to

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.705
really push 'em away.

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:54.206 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they're furious
with America right now,

00:12:54.206 --> 00:12:56.542
as are some of the
other Gulf nations.

00:12:56.542 --> 00:13:01.447 align:start position:0%
They don't see America standing
for moderate Sunni Islam

00:13:02.714 --> 00:13:04.983 align:start size:97% position:3%
the way we promised we
would, and the way we should.

00:13:04.983 --> 00:13:09.254 align:start position:0%
And so, you know, when you
think about the Abraham Accords,

00:13:09.254 --> 00:13:10.522
you tend to think
of it as, you know,

00:13:10.522 --> 00:13:12.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
bilateral relations
between Israel

00:13:12.191 --> 00:13:14.125
and UAE, or Bahrain, or Morocco.

00:13:14.125 --> 00:13:15.761
They're not; it's
a triangle, right?

00:13:15.761 --> 00:13:17.329 align:start size:88% position:13%
Israel and an Arab
country are at the base,

00:13:17.329 --> 00:13:19.731
and the U.S. is at the apex,

00:13:19.731 --> 00:13:21.534
and U.S. plays the
most important role.

00:13:21.534 --> 00:13:23.001
Everybody's looking to the U.S.

00:13:23.001 --> 00:13:24.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
for what they can achieve
in that relationship.

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.872
We're the strongest
country in the world,

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:28.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
we're the most important
country in the world,

00:13:28.139 --> 00:13:30.042
and everybody wants
to be close with us.

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:32.545
And as we push countries away,

00:13:32.545 --> 00:13:34.012
we dilute the Abraham Accords.

00:13:34.012 --> 00:13:36.148
- Right, and if it ain't
us, it's most likely China.

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:37.349
- It's China.

00:13:37.349 --> 00:13:38.284
- And that's a very
different world.

00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:39.551
- Could be, right, I mean, look,

00:13:39.551 --> 00:13:41.687
Saudi's moving closer to
China, Russia, and Iran.

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:42.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's not a
shot against Israel;

00:13:42.888 --> 00:13:44.189
it's a shot against America.

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:45.357
That's a signal to America,

00:13:45.357 --> 00:13:47.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Guys, you know,
this works both ways.

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:48.861
You want to push us away,

00:13:48.861 --> 00:13:50.663
you know, we'll push
you away as well."

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:51.697
- I want to ask you
one other thing,

00:13:51.697 --> 00:13:53.265
because when we got here,

00:13:53.265 --> 00:13:54.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
I really didn't
know what to expect.

00:13:54.834 --> 00:13:56.735
I was bringing my team, we were
gonna tour historical sites,

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:58.838
we were gonna talk
to people like you.

00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:01.440 align:start position:0%
But what I'm realizing now,
just in five days in Jerusalem,

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.309 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that there is an
incredible strength here

00:14:04.309 --> 00:14:07.212 align:start size:97% position:3%
despite the divisions,
despite the security stuff.

00:14:07.212 --> 00:14:10.048
And, you know, you live
in the Promised Land,

00:14:10.048 --> 00:14:11.917 align:start position:0%
and what I would say is the
other promised land of Florida.

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:12.851
(Ambassador Friedman laughs)

00:14:12.851 --> 00:14:15.187
So what is that connection,

00:14:15.187 --> 00:14:17.556
the freedom that's
happening in Florida,

00:14:17.556 --> 00:14:20.092
the freedom and strength
that's happening here,

00:14:20.092 --> 00:14:23.161 align:start size:97% position:3%
to me, that's what has to
be exported to save America.

00:14:23.161 --> 00:14:25.330
Which, you know,
here in Jerusalem,

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.799
this is what every one
of our major cities,

00:14:27.799 --> 00:14:29.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're not gonna
look like geographically,

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:31.970
but the spirit of this
place is incredible,

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.505
and it's so different
than what I'm seeing

00:14:33.505 --> 00:14:35.607 align:start size:97% position:3%
in New York and San Francisco
and all of those places.

00:14:35.607 --> 00:14:38.176
What can Israel export
to the United States

00:14:38.176 --> 00:14:40.145
that might help in
our current crisis?

00:14:40.145 --> 00:14:41.547
- You know what,

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:44.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the most important
thing is meaning,

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.084
a sense of purpose in life,

00:14:46.084 --> 00:14:47.653
that there's a reason
to be on this earth.

00:14:47.653 --> 00:14:51.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we only get, you know, 70,
80, 90 years on this earth.

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:52.925
You want to make it count.

00:14:53.992 --> 00:14:55.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's a real sense
of purpose here,

00:14:55.761 --> 00:14:57.596 align:start size:81% position:19%
that people are
here for a reason.

00:14:57.596 --> 00:14:59.130
They're building something.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.632
They're building something
that matters, that counts.

00:15:00.632 --> 00:15:03.401
They're bringing back to
life Biblical prophecies.

00:15:03.401 --> 00:15:06.438 align:start size:97% position:3%
They're fulfilling, you
know, Judeo-Christian values.

00:15:07.806 --> 00:15:10.776
We've grown untethered from
that in the United States.

00:15:10.776 --> 00:15:12.544
You know, we don't
have relationships,

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:14.713 align:start size:97% position:3%
interpersonal relationships
like we used to.

00:15:14.713 --> 00:15:17.916
People go on dates, you know,
by texting, by WhatsApp-ing.

00:15:17.916 --> 00:15:20.318
I mean, everybody's looking
at their phone all day long.

00:15:20.318 --> 00:15:22.120 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, there's, you know,
they invented the iPhone here,

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.689
so it's not like they
don't do it here too.

00:15:23.689 --> 00:15:24.623
(Dave laughs)

00:15:24.623 --> 00:15:25.924
But it's, there is a sense

00:15:25.924 --> 00:15:28.427
that there's something
bigger than ourselves

00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:30.662
that's driving us forward.

00:15:30.662 --> 00:15:32.798
And I gotta tell you,
when you lose that,

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:36.501 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's a quick trip to the
bottom, it really is.

00:15:36.501 --> 00:15:38.770
I mean, you need to have that
sense of meaning and purpose.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.539
And America had that.

00:15:40.539 --> 00:15:42.741
America was, you
know, it was the,

00:15:42.741 --> 00:15:44.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
for many people, it
was the new Jerusalem.

00:15:44.576 --> 00:15:46.946 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's what our founders
thought about it.

00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.848
They were Christians
who viewed this as the,

00:15:49.848 --> 00:15:52.117 align:start position:0%
you know, as the new Jerusalem,
as the new, you know,

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:53.552
as the shining city on a hill,

00:15:53.552 --> 00:15:55.987 align:start position:0%
as a place of purpose that
would be a light to the nations.

00:15:55.987 --> 00:15:56.889
And

00:15:57.723 --> 00:15:59.258
we don't teach that anymore.

00:15:59.258 --> 00:16:01.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
We don't, people don't
really understand

00:16:01.359 --> 00:16:04.296
why America was created,

00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:05.930
why it's great.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:07.332
And,

00:16:07.332 --> 00:16:10.169
that is, I think, a
very valuable message

00:16:10.169 --> 00:16:11.103
that could come out of Jerusalem

00:16:11.103 --> 00:16:12.838
and the whole state of Israel.

00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:14.139
- Now I have a request for you

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:15.473
that just popped into my head.

00:16:15.473 --> 00:16:16.708
- Sure.

00:16:16.708 --> 00:16:17.910
- What do you say we
do this twice a year?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.346 align:start size:88% position:13%
We do it once in Florida
and once in Israel,

00:16:20.346 --> 00:16:21.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we keep working
this thing out.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:22.814
What do you think?

00:16:22.814 --> 00:16:24.016
- It'd be my pleasure.

00:16:24.016 --> 00:16:25.217 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Thank you, Ambassador.
- Thanks, Dave.

